    "topic": "Bubble wrap was meant to be wallpaper",
    "summary": "In 1957 Alfred Fielding and Marc Chavannes were attempting to create a three-dimensional plastic wallpaper. The idea failed, but they found it could be used as packing material. Fielding co-founded Sealed Air in 1960. One of the first widespread uses came in 1960, shipping IBM 1401 computers to customers who had never seen this packing material. Bubble Wrap Appreciation Day is the last Monday of January, and in 2015 Sealed Air launched iBubble Wrap, which cannot be popped.",
